"""
=======================================================================
  XX International Astronomy Olympiad  (IAO 2015, Kazan)
  Observational round, questions 8-9   (the planetarium)
     8 The Moon   9 Motion of the planets
  Virtual planetarium
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  HaslaLab  /  HaslaEdu        https://haslalab.org
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Single file, Tkinter, Python standard library only.

Design rule (non-negotiable):
    The sheet records only what the planetarium showed and for how
    long; the animations and the solution were not published.  The
    scenes are therefore computed afresh in the same form: question 8
    shows the sky over Kazan (55.8 N, 49.1 E) at the same hour every
    evening, so the stars shift 1 deg a day and the Moon 13 deg;
    question 9 shows the Sun and the planets among the stars with the
    daily motion turned off.  The round runs as on the sheet: reading
    time, two showings (the second paused at the beginning and the
    end), writing time.  No dates or names are shown until the solution
    is opened.  The default scenes are from 2015; "New scene" draws
    others for practice.  The solution is HaslaLab's.

    Run:   python3 iao2015_O_planetarium_EN.py
"""
